 "part_A_threshold_weight": {
  "verdict": {
   "headline": "THE 1.370% BULK MARGIN IS NOT A JUNCTION MARGIN. At the measured tau = 0.80 the Andreev pair-transition energy 2 E_A(phi) drops below h * 145 GHz for |phi| > 0.371293 rad, which is only 0.969 sigma_phi of the E_J/E_C = 100 ground state (sigma_phi = 0.383139 rad). The ground-state phase weight already sitting above the junction threshold AT THE DOME APEX is W = 0.3309 (cosine basis) to 0.3656 (exact-CPR eigenbasis) -- a third of the wavefunction, not a 1.4% margin.",
   "window_verdict": "the ABS-corrected sub-threshold filling window is EMPTY at every audit threshold {1e-3, 1e-2, 0.1}: W(apex) = 0.3309 exceeds all three. The stored bulk window |nu+2.4| < 0.058571 is the region where W rises from 0.3309 to 1, not a region where the drive is safe.",
   "safe_drive_rule": "ABS-corrected safe-drive rule (replaces the bulk margin 2 Delta/h f_d = 1.0139): to hold W(apex) < 1e-3 the drive plane must sit at f_d <= 124.381 GHz (cosine) / 121.506 GHz (exact CPR), i.e. 15.40-17.35% below 2 Delta/h -- margin 1.182-1.210, not 1.014.",
   "scope": "DRIVE-PLANE ONLY, exactly as the bulk audit found. The control (40.597 GHz) and readout (44.597 / 47.597 GHz) tones do not open the ABS channel at all for tau <= 0.8 (they need tau >= 0.924 / 0.908 / 0.895); at tau = 0.95 their W is 1.7e-11 / 5.4e-11 / 1.2e-10, at the charge-basis tail floor. The C5 fork's STRUCTURE survives; its NUMBER does not.",
   "fork_consequence": "qubit.json:allocation.fixed_drive already reads 'EXACTLY 1 CHANNEL'. The ABS audit does not add a channel -- it removes the last one: at 145 GHz there is no ABS-quiet filling at all, so the fixed-drive scenario is not 'one clean qubit', it is 'one qubit with an open, unbounded junction-level pair-breaking channel'. The tracking-drive scenario is unaffected only if each per-qubit tone also respects f_d < f_safe(tau, nu), which is a STRICTER constraint than h f_d < 2 Delta(nu).",
   "claim_limit": "W is a WEIGHT, not a rate. It says the channel is open and how much ground-state phase density is on the open side; it does not say how fast. See parametric_rate for the free-gamma_0 break-even map, and note that this audit is the ABS analogue of the already-flagged qubit.json:open_items.photon_assisted_pair_breaking -- same register, different mechanism."
  },
  "question": "is the 1.370% bulk margin of the 145 GHz drive an artifact of the BULK gap? 2 E_A(phi) = 2 Delta sqrt(1 - tau sin^2(phi/2)) is the junction's own pair-transition energy",
  "definition": {
   "E_A": "E_A(phi, nu) = Delta(nu) sqrt(1 - tau sin^2(phi/2))",
   "W": "W(tau, nu, f_d) = int dphi |psi0(phi)|^2 [2 E_A(phi,nu) < h f_d]",
   "interpretation": "ground-state phase weight sitting where the drive photon is ABOVE the local Andreev pair-transition energy; a threshold+weight audit, NOT a rate",
   "gap_convention_primary": "dome (reproduces the stored bulk window)"
  },
