 "part_B_qp_operator": {
  "verdict": {
   "headline": "THE P3 BRACKETS SURVIVE, BUT ONLY AS A LOWER BOUND. In the design (cosine) eigenbasis the ABS coherence-factor weight raises |<0|sin(phi/2)|1>|^2 from the exported 3.53475392813e-02 by a factor 1.0308 (p=1/4, normalised) to 1.0955 (p=1/2, bare) at tau = 0.8. The parity bracket |<0|cos(phi/2)|0>|^2 moves by at most 2.93%. Relaxation is FASTER: the exported T1 ladder shortens by 3.0-8.7%.",
   "T1_statement": "T1(x_qp = 1e-6, T_qp -> 0) = 5.5200 us -> 5.0387 .. 5.3550 us; the total correction against the milestone-1 small-frequency form grows from the booked x1.172491 to x1.2086 .. x1.2845.",
   "larger_sibling_effect": "A BIGGER effect hides next to it, and it is not the weight: the BARE bracket evaluated in the exact-CPR eigenbasis is 1.1454 times the exported cosine-basis value, because the skewed CPR softens the well (A2 = 0.733) and widens sigma_phi from 0.3831 to 0.4111 rad. Weight and basis together give 1.1856 .. 1.2712. P-extra computed the CPR spectrum but never the qp matrix element, so this number is new -- and it cannot be applied to the exported ladder alone, because the same basis moves f01 to 35.262 GHz.",
   "claim_limit": "the exponent p is a MODEL CHOICE. Both p = 1/4 and p = 1/2 and both normalisation conventions are quoted; nothing here is a single number. Everything stays parametric in x_qp."
  },
  "model": {
   "weight": "(1 - tau sin^2(phi/2))^(-p) = (Delta/E_A(phi))^(2p)",
   "p_values": [
    0.25,
    0.5
   ],
   "status": "MODEL CHOICE, not a measured input",
   "citation": "Catelani, Schoelkopf, Devoret, Glazman, PRB 84, 064517 (2011); Glazman & Catelani, SciPost Phys. Lect. Notes 31 (2021) -- the high-transparency ABS vertex carries coherence factors ~ Delta/E_A(phi); the exponent p is left open and both 1/4 and 1/2 are quoted",
   "convention_A": "bare, anchored at the potential minimum: weight(0) = 1, so the tau -> 0 limit returns the exported tunnel-limit bracket exactly",
   "convention_B": "ground-state normalised: weight / <0|weight|0>, which removes the trivial inflation from weight >= 1 everywhere and isolates the SHAPE correlation"
  },
